{"name":"My Skiff","hex":"#6597ab","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"skiff","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small flat-bottomed open boat with a pointed bow and square stern.","Any of various types of boats small enough for sailing or rowing by one person."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To navigate in a skiff."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/skiff"}],"entries":[{"title":"Skiff","blocks":[{"text":"A skiff is any of a variety of essentially unrelated styles of small boats, usually propelled by sails or oars. Traditionally, these are coastal craft or river craft used for work, leisure, as a utility craft, and for fishing, and have a one-person or small crew. Sailing skiffs have developed into high performance competitive classes. Many of today's skiff classes are based in Australia and New Zealand in the form of 12 ft (3.66 m), 13 ft (3.96 m), 16 ft (4.88 m) and 18 ft (5.49 m) skiffs. The 29er, 49er, SKUD and Musto Skiff are all considered to have developed from the skiff concept, all of which are sailed internationally."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Skiff","wikidata":"Q70744175"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/BoultersLock03.jpg/330px-BoultersLock03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/BoultersLock03.jpg/330px-BoultersLock03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Boulter's Lock, Sunday Afternoon by Edward John Gregory shows skiffs among other craft coming out of the lock","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABoultersLock03.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Skiff.jpg/500px-Skiff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Skiff.jpg/1280px-Skiff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Skiff.jpg/500px-Skiff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Classic flat-bottom skiff in Maine","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASkiff.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Combined_Task_Force_151_-_090211-N-1082Z-111.jpg/500px-Combined_Task_Force_151_-_090211-N-1082Z-111.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Combined_Task_Force_151_-_090211-N-1082Z-111.jpg/1280px-Combined_Task_Force_151_-_090211-N-1082Z-111.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Combined_Task_Force_151_-_090211-N-1082Z-111.jpg/500px-Combined_Task_Force_151_-_090211-N-1082Z-111.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Captured Somalian pirates with their skiff","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACombined_Task_Force_151_-_090211-N-1082Z-111.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Lincoln_Crowne_Skiff_Flying.jpg/500px-Lincoln_Crowne_Skiff_Flying.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Lincoln_Crowne_Skiff_Flying.jpg/500px-Lincoln_Crowne_Skiff_Flying.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Modern 12ft Skiff at speed","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALincoln_Crowne_Skiff_Flying.jpg"}],"sounds":{"skiff":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/dc/En-au-skiff.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcod